\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My God is any hour so sweet,
\par From blush of morn to evening star,
\par As that which calls me Thy feet,
\par The hour of prayer
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Blest be that tranquil hour of morn,
\par And blest that hour of solemn eye,
\par When, on the wings of prayer upborne,
\par The world I leave.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For then a day-spring shines on me,
\par Brighter than morn's ethereal glow;
\par And richer dews descend from Thee
\par Than earth can know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then is my strength by Thee renewed;
\par Then are my sins by Thee forgiven;
\par Then dost Thou cheer mysolitude
\par With hope of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. No words can tell what blest relief,
\par There for my every want I find;
\par What strength for warfare, balm for grief;
\par What peace of mind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Hushed is each doubt, gone every fear;
\par My spirit seems in heaven to stay;
\par And e'en the penitential tear 
\par Is wiped away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Lord, till I reach yon blissful shore,
\par Nor privilege so dear shall be,
\par As thus my inmost soul to pour
\par In prayer to Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

